				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/drewbear" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(301632); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=301632&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607958824" alt="Drewbear" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=301632)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/drewbear" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(301632); return false;" >Drewbear</a></span> <span class="odate time_1340380115 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">22 Jun 2012 15:48</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1487122">
									

<p>Marvel did something similar in their Ultimate Fantastic Four title a few years back. Their version of the Skrulls made &quot;peaceful contact&quot; with Earth and provided us with a pill/easy treatment which would give anyone superpowers. It's implied that everyone on the planet did this and got superpowers except for Ben Grimm (the Thing in normal continuity), so he stayed fully and only human. Then, of course, after having brought over a large number of their people to &quot;further human-Skrull relations and harmony&quot;, they turned off the whatsit that actually powered the superpowers, which killed everyone that had taken the pill/treatment. The Skrulls exploited this to kill the remaining non-pilled superpowered people (it's implied to be 100%, but please. no-one has that perfect a track record), leaving our lovely biome all for themselves. The human Ben Grimm was the only survivor since they couldn't track him with their powers-tracking tech and eventually got hold of some time travel tech and went back to deliberately bork the interdimensional gate which let us contact them, turning the whole thing into a pruned timeline.</p>

							</div>

										<div class="signature">
					<hr class="signature-separator"/>
					

<p>Giving bearhugs to the unsuspecting since 1872.</p>

				</div>
					
					
