															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/trinitite" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1375648); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1375648&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607958825" alt="Trinitite" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1375648)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/trinitite" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1375648); return false;" >Trinitite</a></span> <span class="odate time_1340375673 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">22 Jun 2012 14:34</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1487057">
									

<p>We'd be suspicious about any kind of weapons technology, I think. Quite apart from anything else, giving it to us would imply&#8230;unsettling motives on the aliens' part. Unless one side was naive enough to use it to start a war of TOTAL WORLD CONQUEST MWA-HA-HA leaving them dependent on it to stay in control, I think most advanced nations would make a treaty to only use them against other sides willing to use them. They could give alien superweapons to Kim Jong-Un and force us to take their weapons in self-defence all right, but by that point we'd know that they couldn't be trusted. I was thinking about a point when we literally couldn't survive without alien technology. If the technology was obviously a luxury and the aliens openly turned nasty governments could probably justify pulling out just by telling us how terrifying their demands were. Energy makes sense as a target, medicine maybe less so. I think if the aliens actually demanded our surrender we would turn down their offer of better drugs.</p>
<p>Obviously there's a fine line here: how exploitative does trade have to be before it stops being trade and starts being an invasion/takeover? (Discuss with reference to conflict minerals.) Interesting way of thinking about things. I love this article.</p>

							</div>

								
