					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/thamuzz" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(830521); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=830521&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607958825" alt="thamuzz" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=830521)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/thamuzz" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(830521); return false;" >thamuzz</a></span> <span class="odate time_1340379654 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">22 Jun 2012 15:40</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1487115">
									

<p>Regarding weapons technology specifically:<br />
What about advanced non-lethal weapons technology? Sure, giving out supernukes and lasers that can burn cities to ash in seconds would raise suspicions, but what about a mass produced firearm that could reliably incapacitate an enemy combatant at range without serious threat of injury?<br />
Or maybe instead of weapons, provide defensive equipment that is capable of significantly changing the balance of power?</p>
<p>Expanding on that idea, a good opening move in such a scenario would be for the aliens to offer technologies and goods that people would see as being morally and ethically superior to the goods we have now in addition to any improvements in quality they might offer.</p>

