					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/solan625" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1352778); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1352778&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607958825" alt="Solan625" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1352778)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/solan625" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1352778); return false;" >Solan625</a></span> <span class="odate time_1340392176 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">22 Jun 2012 19:09</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1487311">
									

<p>I like this. I <em>really</em> like this. I have one slight quibble though&#8230; you mention the aliens could initiate an ADANA event via medical, industrial, or military avenues&#8230; what about just commercial ones? Think about it, even now we're barely able to function without a -lot- of cheap commercial products (laptops and cellphones, to take a very vital example). There's a lot more than just &quot;vital&quot; technologies that we could become dependent on&#8230; not to mention, a large part of the world operates under capitalist principles. Even if we could &quot;wean ourselves off&quot;, they'd still have enough cash to simultaneously rig every election in the world and bribe the candidate of their choice into basically capitulating. This obviously wouldn't work in places like Russia or China, but huge chunks of the free world effectively conquered just by selling a bunch of cheap knicknacks? That's pretty dang scary too.</p>

							</div>

								
					
