					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/wishun" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1204404); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1204404&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607958825" alt="wishun" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1204404)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/wishun" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1204404); return false;" >wishun</a></span> <span class="odate time_1340739850 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">26 Jun 2012 19:44</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1491038">
									

<p>For examples of this strategy using multiple fields (medicine, industry, weapons, etc.) simultaneously see Earth Final Conflict.<br />
I think an overt strategy would work better than a covert one. It is very hard to achieve the market saturation neccessary for such a plan without someone getting curious about where this new wonder-tech is coming from. And if exposed, a covert strategy immediately casts doubt on the intentions of the aliens and begins the public distrust that this protocol would attempt to sow.</p>
<p>What does &quot;ADANA&quot; stand for? Did I just miss it?</p>

							</div>

								
					
